#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068650 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00d1bec1-5f96-5ea9-863e-8f7312c8b526" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of the Cube Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "efb469e0-ae96-553d-8e7a-56a25739e4af" :question/math-academy-id "e-7942" :question/problem "![](images/06/06a54157969bfc559c8622512bca59b796f8100f8b52542165acb1eb2f397585.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}{:}$\n\n- The point $(0,0)$ lies on the graph.\n\n- Its domain is $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\n- Its range is $y\\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\n- The graph lies in the first and third quadrants.\n\n- The function is increasing throughout its entire domain.\n\n- As $x \\rightarrow \\infty,$ we have $y\\rightarrow \\infty,$ though the function increases more slowly as $x$ gets large.\n\n- As $x \\rightarrow -\\infty,$ we have $y\\rightarrow -\\infty,$  though the function decreases more slowly as $x$ becomes very negative.\n\nOf the given options, only graph I has all of the above properties. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068651 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3135b492-14a6-5ccf-9b83-deecba63f7f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of the Cube Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "289fd11d-ce6d-5554-a061-9647c67e5326" :question/math-academy-id "e-7943" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x) =\\sqrt[3]{x}?$\n\nI. The point $(64,4)$ lies on the graph of $y=f(x)$\n\nII. The domain of $f(x)$ is $x\\in[-1,\\infty)$\n\nIII. $f(x) \\rightarrow -\\infty$ as $x \\rightarrow -\\infty$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by recalling the graph of $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}.$\n\n![](images/ab/abafb7d55b4baa0b06f20c3de2b44d5925f7286f078aaa76d71aded7c9c9a001.png)\n\nNow, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $f(64)=\\sqrt[3]{64}=4.$\n\n- Statement II is false since $f(x) =\\sqrt[3]{x}$ is defined for $x \\in (-\\infty, \\infty).$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $f(x) \\rightarrow -\\infty$ as $x \\rightarrow -\\infty.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527185 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3135b492-14a6-5ccf-9b83-deecba63f7f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of the Cube Root Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e8a624a-766c-5521-a7e0-68fa10357b2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526567} {:answer/id #uuid "46095390-0a49-5a60-94b9-d4b2808b83a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526637} {:answer/id #uuid "955053f1-ca40-507d-adfd-f164744f1aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526795} {:answer/id #uuid "e7dc61b4-da33-58f5-acc1-5cb4210241cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526961} {:answer/id #uuid "ff18e589-7302-5c48-9ca4-e66cc9290084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e8a624a-766c-5521-a7e0-68fa10357b2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526567} :answer-field/id #uuid "61b564d7-3dd3-5be8-b00c-7d4c0105b021" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radi