t :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "90b71102-b1fe-54a8-9326-1ad18a9d698b" :question/math-academy-id "q-89855" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}?$\n\nI. The range of $f(x)$ is $(-10,\\infty )$\n\nII. $f(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty $\n\nIII. The graph of $f(x)$ lies in the second and fourth quadrants" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by recalling the graph of $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}.$\n\n![](images/ab/abafb7d55b4baa0b06f20c3de2b44d5925f7286f078aaa76d71aded7c9c9a001.png)\n\nNow, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false since the range of $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, $f(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\n- Statement III is false since the graph of $f(x)$ lies in the first and third quadrants\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}]}
